trikes in the turn he starts it rather than telegraphing it. ","type":"text"},{"code":"I-FIGHT","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clears the bit on the villain the player is no longer standing with, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"walking out ends a fight and walking back in asks the question again.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Neither 0 nor 100 draws; see ","type":"text"},{"code":"startsAFight(chance:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"while:"},{"type":"text","text":" is an extra gate evaluated before the same-room guard and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before any draw — so a villain whose combat is scoped (the thief only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fights in his lair) burns no randomness on the turns his gate is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closed, keeping every seeded draw sequence intact. It does "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coming round, which happens first: a man knocked out where his gate is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shut still wakes up. Nor does it gate "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"disengaging","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", which is the room’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"business rather than the host’s — the source agrees, skipping the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"engrossed thief’s turn without clearing his "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FIGHTBIT"},{"type":"text","text":" — so a man"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"admiring a gift you handed him is still in the fight when he looks up."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Gates are assumed pure: they are asked once per turn and their answer is"},{"type":"tex